#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:0
msgid ""
"Understand how Intel RST RAID can block disk detection in the Ubuntu "
"installer, and how to resolve it by turning off RST or switching to AHCI."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:8
msgid "Topics: Installation Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:12
msgid "Intel RST during Ubuntu installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:14
msgid ""
"Intel Rapid Storage Technology (RST) is a solution built into a range of "
"Intel chipsets. On platforms that have RST support built and enabled in the "
"firmware (BIOS or UEFI), RST enables users to group and manage multiple "
"disks as a single volume. This functionality is known as the Redundant Array "
"of Independent Disks (RAID)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:16
msgid ""
"RAID offers various advantages over the use of several independent disks. "
"RAID supports multiple configurations (*levels*) which focus on performance "
"and redundancy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:19
msgid "RST with Ubuntu and Windows"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:21
msgid ""
"If you want to install Ubuntu on a computer that uses RST, you might have to "
"make adjustments to your setup first."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:23
msgid ""
"The Ubuntu installer can detect certain RAID configurations, but it might "
"not be able to access the disks grouped in them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:25
msgid ""
"If the Ubuntu installer can't detect the disks that you need, you must turn "
"off RST in the computer’s firmware before you can install Ubuntu. The "
"terminology and steps to access and manage RST in the firmware depend on the "
"implementation by the platform vendor. For instance, Dell, Lenovo and HP "
"computers all have different settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:27
msgid ""
"Furthermore, Windows might be already installed on the computer that uses "
"RST. If you disable RST in the firmware or change the RST configuration, "
"Windows might become unable to start because it's no longer able to find the "
"disks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:30
msgid "Possible installation scenarios"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:32
msgid ""
"Broadly, you might encounter the following configurations when you try to "
"install Ubuntu on a computer that uses RST:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:37
msgid "RST state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:38
msgid "Operating system state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:40
msgid "RST enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:41
#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:44
msgid "No operating system installed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:43
#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:46
msgid "RST used and enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:47
msgid "Windows installed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:50
msgid ""
"Based on the configuration, the following installation scenarios are "
"possible:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:52
msgid "When Ubuntu can access the disks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:54
msgid "The Ubuntu installer **correctly detects** the disks and can use them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:56
msgid "In this case, you can proceed with the Ubuntu installation as usual."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:58
msgid ""
"If Windows is installed on the system, you need to create a side-by-side "
"configuration for Windows and Ubuntu."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:60
msgid "When Ubuntu can't access the disks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:62
msgid ""
"The Ubuntu installer **detects a conflict** with RST and notifies you that "
"manual configuration is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:64
msgid "You can resolve this problem by either one of the following changes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:66
msgid "Turn off RST completely in the firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:68
msgid ""
"Change the storage controller protocol from RST to Advanced Host Controller "
"Interface (AHCI)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:70
msgid ""
"If Windows is installed, the change will affect the Windows operating system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:72
msgid ""
"To switch the Windows storage controller from RST to AHCI, see {ref}"
"`reconfigure-windows-to-use-ahci`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:75
msgid ""
"Changes to storage configuration might lead to irrecoverable loss of data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:77
msgid "If you break a RAID setup, your data might no longer be accessible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:79
msgid ""
"If you change the controller type from RST to AHCI, Windows might no longer "
"be able to boot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:83
msgid "AHCI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:85
msgid ""
"AHCI is a specification that describes how computer storage is accessed and "
"managed. It supersedes several legacy specifications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:87
msgid ""
"It is designed to use advanced features of disks connected via the Serial "
"ATA (SATA) bus. Typically, these are 2.5\" or 3.5\" disks, either mechanical "
"hard drives or SSD devices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:89
msgid ""
"The change from RST to AHCI might result in the loss of some of the advanced "
"functionality that the RST module offers: for instance TRIM for SSD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/intel-rst-during-ubuntu-installation.md:91
msgid ""
"The terminology and steps to access and manage controller type in the "
"firmware depend on the specific implementation by the platform vendor."
msgstr ""
